        )
        self.solution.append(
            "The impact can vary with the source of the comments and the setting. Remarks from a close family member, partner, teacher, supervisor, or peer group may carry added weight because these relationships often shape belonging and self-image. Isolation, power differences, public humiliation, and a long duration of exposure may deepen the emotional effect. Supportive relationships and access to care can help a person recover their sense of self."
        )
        self.solution.append(
            "Across history, demeaning language has appeared in bullying, coercive relationships, hostile workplace cultures, discriminatory campaigns, and propaganda. It has been used to portray targets as lesser, create shame, weaken social ties, and make unfair treatment appear ordinary. Recognizing these patterns helps communities respond with respect, accountability, and care."
        )
        self.solution.append(
            "Helpful responses include documenting patterns, setting clear boundaries where safe, spending time with trusted people, and using affirming language that separates a person's value from the harmful remarks. A counselor, therapist, school support professional, or community advocate can offer tailored guidance and coping tools. Immediate support from local emergency services or a crisis resource may be appropriate when a person faces urgent danger or thoughts of self-harm."
