        self.sub_tasks.append(
            "Study practical pathways countries may use to operate around NPT obligations, such as treaty interpretation, withdrawal provisions, loopholes, non-compliance disputes, and strategic ambiguity."
        )
        self.sub_tasks.append(
            "Compare official treaty text, diplomatic statements, research reports, and policy analyses from government agencies and international organizations."
        )
        self.sub_tasks.append(
            "Organize findings into a clear briefing that explains the NPT, current pressures on the treaty, and possible workaround strategies countries may attempt."
        )

    def generate_solution(self):
        self.solution.append(
            "Define the research goal as a focused study of the NPT treaty, its obligations, and the strategies states may use to reduce or avoid those obligations. Use this goal to guide source selection and the final briefing structure."
        )
        self.solution.append(
            "Provide the NPT background: opened for signature in 1968, entered into force in 1970, built around three pillars of non-proliferation, disarmament, and peaceful uses of nuclear energy. Describe the review conferences, the IAEA safeguards role, and the near-universal membership with notable states outside the treaty."
        )
        self.solution.append(
            "Explain the main obligations: non-nuclear-weapon states commit not to receive or manufacture nuclear weapons and to accept safeguards; nuclear-weapon states commit to pursue negotiations on disarmament; all parties commit to peaceful nuclear cooperation and to refrain from helping others acquire nuclear weapons."
        )
        self.solution.append(
            "Outline the concern about rule-following: some states may resist full compliance due to security interests, alliance pressures, regional rivalries, or domestic politics. The USA and Russia hold special status as nuclear-weapon states and major world powers, so their actions, interpretations, and bilateral relations strongly shape how other countries view the treaty."
        )
        self.solution.append(
            "List and explain possible workaround pathways: invoking the Article X withdrawal clause with advance notice; using civilian nuclear programs in ways that raise safeguards concerns; delaying disarmament commitments; interpreting obligations narrowly; forming nuclear-sharing arrangements; pursuing dual-use technologies; challenging verification access; and using diplomatic forums to contest compliance findings."
        )
        self.solution.append(
            "Create a source comparison table with columns for source type, key claim, supporting evidence, and relevance to NPT obligations or workaround pathways. Use official NPT text, UN and IAEA materials, government policy papers, academic research, and reputable news analyses."
        )
        self.solution.append(
            "Write the final briefing in sections: NPT overview, key obligations, current pressures involving major powers, possible workaround strategies, case examples, and conclusions. Add citations, dates, and a short glossary so the research is useful for a government agency audience."
        )
